## Summary

### New functionality in `src/commands_dev.rs`:

1. `toolchain_checks_for_project()` function — Returns project-type-specific toolchain version checks:
   • Java: Checks java --version, `JAVA_HOME env var, and mvn --version or gradle --version` (based on whether pom.xml exists)
   • Ruby: Checks ruby --version, bundle --version, gem --version
   • Cpp: Checks cmake --version, make --version, and compiler (cc --version with fallback to `g++ --version`)

2. Integration into `run_doctor_checks()` — Added step 12 that detects the project type and appends toolchain checks, so running /doctor in a Java/Ruby/C++ project shows relevant toolchain diagnostics.

3. **`check_tool() helper** — DRY inner function that runs a command and returns a DoctorCheck` with Pass (including version string) or Fail status.

### 15 new tests:

• Health check coverage: `test_health_checks_for_java_project, test_health_checks_for_ruby_project, test_health_checks_for_cpp_project, test_health_checks_for_make_project`
• Toolchain checks: `test_toolchain_checks_java, test_toolchain_checks_ruby, test_toolchain_checks_cpp, test_toolchain_checks_unknown_empty, test_toolchain_checks_rust_empty`
• Doctor infrastructure: test_doctor_status_equality, `test_doctor_check_construction, test_run_doctor_checks_structure, test_print_doctor_report_all_pass, test_print_doctor_report_mixed_statuses`, test_print_doctor_report_empty

